Bringing in an interim coach will sometimes light a fire underneath the players on the team. The offensive coordinator gets a long overdue promotion. The tight ends coach who was previously the head honcho gets put back into the spotlight. Jeff Saturday gets brought off his couch. That can really get the guys going. Usually. Recently speaking at least, the first game bump has not been super kind to the freshly wounded. And in those occasions where the interim coach gets his first win in his first game, that looks awful bad on the loser.


