About half the time, those teams are able to win that first game. The schedule sometimes will dictate that though. The 2024 Bears and Jets both got beat by perennial playoff contenders. The Saints, on the other hand, took down a Falcons team that’s been in football purgatory since 28-3.
But for those teams that can’t get that win in Game 1, the rest of the tenure must look okay, right? Well…that isn’t really the case. Over this sample size, interim coaches are winning games at just a 31.2% clip. Over the longer interim stints that these replacement coaches have, those results don’t show up. The shorter stints look better.


Code
interims &lt;- bind_rows(b_10broncos_int, b_10cowboys_int, b_10niners_int, b_10vikings_int, b_11chiefs_int, b_11dolphins_int, b_11jaguars_int, b_12saints_int, b_13texans_int, b_14raiders_int, b_15dolphins_int, b_15eagles_int, b_15titans_int, b_16bills_int, b_16jaguars_int, b_16rams_int, b_17giants_int, b_18browns_int, b_18packers_int, b_19commanders_int, b_19panthers_int, b_20falcons_int, b_20lions_int, b_20texans_int, b_21jaguars_int, b_21raiders_int, b_22broncos_int, b_22colts_int, b_22panthers_int, b_23chargers_int, b_23panthers_int, b_23raiders_int, b_24bears_int, b_24jets_int, b_24saints_int) |&gt; 
  filter(Team != "NA") |&gt; 
  mutate(Outcome = if_else(Rslt == "W", "Win", "Loss"))

summary_outcomes &lt;- interims |&gt;
  count(TeamSeason, Outcome)

total_games &lt;- summary_outcomes |&gt; 
  group_by(TeamSeason) |&gt; 
  summarize(
    TotalGames = sum(n)
  )

summary_outcomes &lt;- summary_outcomes |&gt; 
  left_join(total_games)

ggplot() +
  geom_bar(data=summary_outcomes, aes(x=reorder(TeamSeason, TotalGames), weight=n, fill= Outcome)) +
  coord_flip(
  ) +
  scale_fill_manual(
    values = c(
      "Win" = "darkgreen",
      "Loss" = "red"
  )) +
  scale_y_continuous(limits = c(0, 12), breaks = seq(0, 12, by = 2)
  ) +
  labs(
    x="Team and Season", 
    y="Total Games", 
    title="Interim coaches don't have the highest win rate in the world.", 
    subtitle="There is an awful lot of red on this chart. Except for the 2021 Raiders. That was fun.", 
    caption="By: Danny Berg | Source: SportsReference"
  ) +
  theme_minimal(
  ) +
  theme(
    plot.title = element_text(size = 16, face = "bold"),
    axis.title = element_text(size = 10), 
    plot.subtitle = element_text(size=10), 
    panel.grid.minor = element_blank(),
    plot.title.position = "plot",
    axis.text.y=element_text(size=6)
  ) 









If the interim isn’t doing super hot, then the guy that was there beforehand didn’t do super well either (usually). The team is just not good. The offense might be good but the defense doesn’t exist. The defense might be electric but the offense can’t get a touchdown if their lives depended on it. Or maybe everything is bad! The point differentials usually are not going to look great.

On the left of the blue line represents the coach that began the season at the helm. The blue line itself represents their final game. A vast majority of the canned coaches were having a hard time staying at the break-even point. When the losses stack up, that point differential nosedives. Surprisingly, though, a lot of teams clean it up after moving out of an office.


Code
master &lt;- bind_rows(bears_24, bills_16, broncos_10, broncos_22, browns_18, chargers_23, chiefs_11, colts_22, commanders_19, cowboys_10, dolphins_11, dolphins_15, eagles_15, falcons_20, giants_17, jaguars_11, jaguars_16, jaguars_21, jets_24, lions_20, niners_10, packers_18, panthers_19, panthers_22, panthers_23, raiders_14, raiders_21, raiders_23, rams_16, saints_12, saints_24, texans_13, texans_20, titans_15, vikings_10) |&gt; 
